==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|fro|receptacle}}, from {{der|en|la|receptāculum||reservoir, receptacle}}, from {{m|la|receptō||I receive back or again, recover}}, frequentative of {{m|la|recipiō||I receive; hold back, reserve}}, from {{m|la|re-||back, again}} + {{m|la|capiō||I hold}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[container]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} The part of the [[flower]] [[stalk]] ([[peduncle]] or [[pedicel]]) to which the floral parts are attached; also [[torus]].
## In the ''[[Asteraceae]]'', the end of the peduncle to which all of the florets of the flower head are attached.
# {{lb|en|electricity|US}} A contact device installed at an [[outlet]] for the connection of an attachment plug and flexible cord to supply portable equipment or appliances.

